panero (0.1.0~preview.10-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Tenth preview (git tag v0.1.0-preview.10).
  * Fix: the window could freeze while browsing a cloud drive when rclone was
    busy (for example opening files for another program): Panero touched the
    drive from its GUI thread (working directory, folder watcher, custom
    folder icons, the folder tree). It no longer does.
  * Google Drive, OneDrive, Dropbox, Box: no forced re-read of the shown
    folder every 30 s (rclone polls these providers; the re-read locked the
    folder for the whole network listing).
  * New freeze test with a stopped rclone (dev/scripts/gui-cloud-freeze-test.sh).

 -- Norbert Szabo <349977413+NorbCraft@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:00:00 +0100

panero (0.1.0~preview.9-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Ninth preview (git tag v0.1.0-preview.9).
  * Cloud drives: the whole folder list is read in the background after
    connecting; folders are read in a worker thread (no freezes) and checked
    for changes in the background; Ctrl+R re-reads one folder.
  * Google Drive: optional own client ID (rclone's shared one is rate
    limited); the secret is stored through rclone's private socket.
  * Folder badge when everything inside is offline; Rename for cloud drives;
    browsing stops at the drive's top folder.
  * rclone remote control only on a private unix socket with hashed
    per-mount credentials.

 -- Norbert Szabo <349977413+NorbCraft@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 22 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0100

panero (0.1.0~preview.8-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Eighth preview (git tag v0.1.0-preview.8).
  * Cloud drives browse much faster: no file is opened to guess its type,
    free space is cached, folder listings are kept (with change polling) and
    the next folder level is listed ahead; Ctrl+R fetches a folder again.
  * Make Available Offline and Free Up Space for files and folders.
  * Google Docs/Sheets/Slides open in the browser; save an Office copy.
  * Progress windows while a cloud drive is set up and while it connects.

