panero (0.1.0~preview.5-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Fifth preview (git tag v0.1.0-preview.5): safe cloud sign-in
    (dev/CLOUD-SECURITY-AUDIT.md).
  * Ships its own rclone 1.76.0 (pinned, checksum-verified upstream build)
    instead of using Ubuntu's 1.60.1, which is affected by CVE-2026-116194.
  * Cloud sign-ins are kept in Panero's own rclone configuration, encrypted;
    the key is in the desktop keyring. No secret on command lines.
  * Remove signs out at the provider where possible; Sign Out of All Clouds.
  * Sign-in explains the access granted; read-only and narrower OneDrive
    access; MEGA no longer in the guided list; import from rclone.
  * Offline files: opened files stay available, Keep on This Device, Free Up
    Space, badges in the panels.

